From 2dd5351d2d969995826adb937a61aadb9836b9ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronan Silva <ronansilva755@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:21:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ui: make tunnel startup configurable
To: wireguard@lists.zx2c4.com

Tunnel services currently use automatic startup, so an active tunnel is
started again after Windows reboots even if the user intended to activate
it only for the current session.

Add a Start with Windows checkbox to the create/edit dialog and save the
preference with each tunnel. Store the preference in a comment before the
Interface section so exported configurations remain compatible with other
WireGuard clients. Preserve it through parsing, serialization, renaming,
export/import, and runtime configuration queries.

Create tunnel services with manual startup by default, and select automatic
startup when a tunnel is activated from the UI with this option enabled.
The installtunnelservice command also defaults to manual startup. Existing
installed services retain their startup setting until they are reinstalled
or deactivated and activated again from the UI. Deactivating a tunnel still
removes its service and prevents startup at the next boot.

This intentionally changes the default for configurations without the new
preference from automatic to manual startup. The manager service continues
to use automatic startup.

Add preference parsing and round-trip tests, update the enterprise
documentation, and provide English and Portuguese UI strings.

Validation:
- go test ./conf -skip '^TestStorage$' -count=1
- go build -o .deps/wireguard-check.exe .
- git diff --check

Real Windows reboot behavior has not yet been tested.

Signed-off-by: Ronan Silva <ronansilva755@gmail.com>
